      "body_plain": "Hi.\n\nLeadership is key for human well being. I can guide on this opportunity.\n\nRegards,\nVinit\n\nSent from BlackBerry® on Airtel\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: bhalchandra bhutkar <bhutkar.b...@gmail.com>\nSender: bru...@googlegroups.com\nDate: Thu, 9 Feb 2012 00:25:43\nTo: Bangalore R Users - BRU<bru...@googlegroups.com>\nReply-To: bru...@googlegroups.com\nSubject: About Ordinal logistic regression\n\nHi all,\nI am a kind of beginner for the R tool . I have a data of a survey of\na particular city which include \" Gender \" ,\" Age \" and \" Reading\nHabbit \" and \" Leadership Vision \" . I want to perform ordinal\nlogistic regression on this data where\n\n 1. Output variable is leasership vision ( Ordinal ) its values ranges\nfrom 0 to 6\n2. Gender takes values 1 for male and 2 for female\n3. Age is a continuous variable\n4. Reading habbit is a ordinal variable with values ranging from 1 to\n4.\n\nSo I want to fit a model which talks about the combined effect of\n\"Gender \" ,\" Age\" and \"Reading Habbit\" on the resulting variable that\nis \" Leadership Vision \"\n\nI am using a function \" Polr.out\" of R . But I am unable to understand\nthe output of that particular function . Can anybody please help me\nregarding the output of that function.\n\nOne more thing library(Design) package is not available for R\nanymore . So any is alternative package which does work of Design\npackage",
