      "body_plain": "Hi,\n\nI have explored quantmod package but it takes symbols from yahoo or google. Is there any way to access symbols which are stored in Mysql DB using quantmod package?\n\nRegards,\nAshy\n\nOn Sat, Feb 18, 2012 at 2:23 PM, <vinit....@gmail.com> wrote:\n> Hi Ashy.\n>\n> Haven't used quantmod-MySql, but consider RMySQL to access db, and once data is within (dframe in) R, use quantmod pkg.\n>\n> Regards,\n> Vinit\n>\n> Sent from BlackBerry® on Airtel\n>\n> -----Original Message-----\n> From: Ashy <a.na...@gmail.com>\n> Sender: bru...@googlegroups.com\n> Date: Thu, 2 Feb 2012 23:48:53\n> To: Bangalore R Users - BRU<bru...@googlegroups.com>\n> Reply-To: bru...@googlegroups.com\n> Subject: DB connection in quantmod\n>\n> Hi All,\n>\n> Currently I am using R 2.14.0 version in which RMySQL package is\n> available to establish connection with MySql database. I want to use\n> 'quantmod' package which is use for stock charts. Could anyone tell\n> how to establish connection to MySQL DB in quantmod package? I have\n> tried but got the following error-\n>\n> Quantmod / xts problem \" Error in `[.xts`(x, xsubset) : subscript out\n> of bounds\"",
